// CotSC Batch 18 - extracted original English dialogue for nashkel_citizens.d
// Keep existing @ numbers stable when translating.
@1 = ~Nothing better than clearing your mind whilst fishing.~
@2 = ~Why do I always struggle with catching fish. Either too small, or none at all. I'm practically a a laughing stock.~
@3 = ~I know my husband hated flowers but I like to think he appreciates the gesture of me putting some on his grave every now and then.~
@4 = ~Business with the mines really put something out in me. My brother used to work as a miner before… he perished. Guards said they looked but he was never found. But I know what happened. These awful creatures that dwell down there killed him.~
@5 = ~Would you believe this Noober guy has a family who apparently is just as infuriating as he is? No? I don't believe so either. No one can be worse.~
@6 = ~You look hardened. Check out the carnival east from here. There are bound to be some attractions that will take your mind off the troubles that bother you. I can tell there's a lot of such trouble on our head.~
@7 = ~I wish I was as brave as you. Shiny armor, magical weapons and spells. I'd be far more invested in this than my current boring life as a farmer.~
@8 = ~Some nights ago I saw a few kobolds, here on the fields. I got so spooked I spent the whole night holding a crossbow, snuggled up in the corner of my room. I know not all of them are bad. I even spoke to one that was restocking his supplies at the local shop but let's just say I've heard some real nasty stories about them recently.~
